       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Sertraline 400 mg daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 200 mg/day for adults. Higher doses carry a greater risk of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, GI bleeding, and hyponatremia, and I know of no evidence that they work better. Your patient's normal renal and hepatic function and lack of allergies don't change that limit.\n\nWhich of these do you want?\n1. **Enter 200 mg PO once daily**, the maximum labeled dose. Or I can enter a lower starting dose, such as 50 mg daily, if the patient is starting treatment.\n2. **Enter 400 mg PO daily as written.** This would be an intentional off-label order. Please confirm that's what you want, and tell me if you'd like a note on the order, such as the rationale or monitoring plan.\n3. **Change something else.** The 400 mg may have been a typo, or you may have meant a different drug or dose.\n\nTell me which one and I'll enter it right away."
